- op: update  # 1eac
  at: '2026-10-29T18:34:58Z'  # 1eac
  by: agent  # 1eac
  actor: jgstern_agent  # 1eac
  clock: 5  # 1eac
  nonce: 1eac  # 1eac
  set:  # 1eac
    title: "yjs: a function that point-reads a shared-map entry (yMap.get) is not linked to the entry's writer, so PlazaFlow's SpatialObject -> session-doc flow is invisible"  # 1eac
    description: "## The PlazaFlow flow this is about\n\nPlazaFlow spec (~/plazaflow/spec.md §4.2, §5.3, §5.4): every interactive thing is a\n`SpatialObject` stored in the chunk doc's `objects` Y.Map, carrying a `yjsDocId`; a\nclient reads the object and connects to the separate Y.Doc that id names. In code:\n\n    // writer (§5.4)\n    chunk.getMap(\"objects\").set(id, { id, type: \"collab\", x, y, yjsDocId });\n    // reader (§5.3)\n    const obj = chunk.getMap(\"objects\").get(id);\n    const sessionDoc = new Y.Doc({ guid: obj.yjsDocId });\n    new WebsocketProvider(url, obj.yjsDocId, sessionDoc);\n\n## What hypergumbo does with it today (dev 4401fbfa30)\n\nThe yjs-crdt linker links a WRITER of a shared type (`.set` / `.delete` /\n`getMap('name')`) to an OBSERVER (`.observe` / `.observeDeep`, awareness, BlockSuite\nslots) through `event_publishes` on the shared-type name. A point READ,\n`yMap.get(key)`, is neither, so the function that reads the SpatialObject and opens\nits session doc has no edge from the function that wrote it. A forward slice from the\nwriter never reaches the session code; a reverse slice from the session code never\nfinds who created the object.\n\n## Acceptance\n\n- Fixture (the four-line flow above; ~/hypergumbo_lab_notebook/munok_10292026/fixture):\n  an edge from `startCollab` (writer) to `joinCollab` (reader), alongside the existing\n  `startCollab` -> `watchObjects` (observer) edge.\n- A read of a key nobody writes stays unlinked; reads of other maps do not link.\n- Corpus A/B on the Yjs repos (plazaflow_deep_repos/cohort2_yjs: AFFiNE, blocksuite,\n  hocuspocus, yjs, y-sweet, y-webrtc, y-websocket) with every new edge read: `.get(`\n  is a common method name, so the read must be anchored on a receiver bound to a\n  shared type (`getMap(...)` result), as the write side is.\n\n## Out of scope\n\n- An edge to a \"Yjs document node\": hypergumbo has no node for a runtime Y.Doc\n  instance, and the doc id is a runtime string (`sess-${id}`), so the\n  object -> document hop has no static channel. The original filing asked for this\n  (`document_references`, an edge type that does not exist); see the 2026-10-29 note.\n- General Yjs API surface: WI-zusig (done) and WI-mamuh (done).\n\n## No real-code substrate\n\nPlazaFlow is spec-only: ~/plazaflow holds spec.md, essentialized.md and research\nnotes, no product code; no repo in plazaflow_deep_repos or plazaflow_focused_mar15\ncontains `yjsDocId` or `SpatialObject`. The fixture is the evidence until PlazaFlow\nhas code.\n\nHistory: filed 2026-05-14 from a META-sulor cross-reference; re-scoped 2026-10-29."  # 1eac
    fields:  # 1eac
      statement: "A function that point-reads a Yjs shared-type entry (yMap.get(key) on a receiver bound by getMap/getArray) is linked to the function that writes that shared type, as an observer of it already is. The runtime object -> Y.Doc hop (yjsDocId is a runtime string) is out of scope."  # 1eac
      root_cause: "The yjs-crdt linker's read patterns are observe/observeDeep (plus awareness and BlockSuite slots). A point read yMap.get(key) is neither a publisher nor a subscriber, so the function that reads a SpatialObject and opens the Y.Doc its yjsDocId names has no edge from the function that wrote the object. Measured on a spec-shaped fixture 2026-10-29 (dev 4401fbfa30)."  # 1eac
- op: discuss  # f1c3
  at: '2026-10-29T18:34:59Z'  # f1c3
  by: agent  # f1c3
  actor: jgstern_agent  # f1c3
  clock: 6  # f1c3
  nonce: f1c3  # f1c3
  message: "PREMISE CHECK 2026-10-29 (dev 4401fbfa30). Re-scoped: title, statement, root_cause, description. Status stays violated, now with a repro; P4 unchanged.\n\nWHAT WAS WRONG WITH THE FILING\n1. It asked for an edge \"from the SpatialObject node to the referenced Yjs document node\", type `document_references`. Neither exists: no edge type `document_references` anywhere in packages/*/src, and hypergumbo mints no node for a runtime Y.Doc instance or a CRDT entry (the yjs-crdt linker's nodes are crdt_publisher / crdt_subscriber stand-ins anchored on code). The doc id is a runtime string, so object -> document has no static channel.\n2. Status `violated` was asserted without a repro (\"violated until empirically demonstrated otherwise\"; root_cause \"Unknown pending empirical investigation\").\n3. Stale: the acceptance called WI-zusig `todo_soft`; it is done (it is this item's parent). PR #2329 / #2256 are Forgejo-era numbers, not the current GitHub PRs.\n4. The shape has no substrate: ~/plazaflow is spec-only (spec.md 2026-03-15; no code), and grep for yjsDocId|SpatialObject across ~/ALL_REPOS/plazaflow_deep_repos and plazaflow_focused_mar15 finds nothing.\n\nREPRO (fixture following spec §4.2/§5.3/§5.4; saved at ~/hypergumbo_lab_notebook/munok_10292026/fixture):\n  src/world.ts    startCollab: chunk.getMap(\"objects\").set(id, {..., yjsDocId})\n  src/session.ts  joinCollab:  chunk.getMap(\"objects\").get(id) -> new Y.Doc({guid: obj.yjsDocId}); new WebsocketProvider(url, obj.yjsDocId, doc); doc.getText(\"main.py\")\n                  watchObjects: chunk.getMap(\"objects\").observe(render)\n`hypergumbo survey` (exit 0), yjs-crdt-linker edges:\n  event_publishes src/world.ts:8 objects:crdt_publisher -> src/session.ts:13 yjs:crdt_subscriber\n  uses startCollab -> objects:crdt_publisher ; uses watchObjects -> yjs:crdt_subscriber\n  joinCollab: only plain `calls` to getMap/get/getText and module_attr_ref yjs.Doc -- no edge from startCollab.\nSo writer -> observer links and writer -> point-reader does not: the linker's read patterns are observe/observeDeep (+awareness, BlockSuite slots), and `yMap.get(key)` is not one.\n\nRE-SCOPED STATEMENT: a function that point-reads a Yjs shared-type entry is linked to the function that writes it, as an observer is. The object -> document hop is out of scope and stated so."  # f1c3
