- op: discuss  # 14a2
  at: '2026-10-29T19:45:42Z'  # 14a2
  by: agent  # 14a2
  actor: jgstern_agent  # 14a2
  clock: 8  # 14a2
  nonce: 14a2  # 14a2
  message: "SATISFIED (re-scoped statement of 2026-10-29). Fixed in PR #1942 (dev 38f9ffbd84).\n\nFiled repro re-run on merged dev: `hypergumbo survey ~/hypergumbo_lab_notebook/munok_10292026/fixture` (exit 0), event_publishes edges:\n  startCollab [yjs.write(objects) src/world.ts:8] -> watchObjects [yjs.observe(yjs) src/session.ts:13]   (as before)\n  startCollab [yjs.set(objects.*) src/world.ts:8] -> joinCollab [yjs.get(objects.*) src/session.ts:6]    (NEW; absent before the fix)\nSo the function that creates the SpatialObject now reaches the one that reads it back and opens the Y.Doc its yjsDocId names.\n\nFix: yjs-crdt linker entry sites -- .set/.delete/.push/.insert/.unshift (write) and .get/.has/.toJSON/.toArray/.forEach/.entries/.values/.keys (read) on a receiver that IS a shared type (chained getMap('x')/getArray('x'), generic or not, or a name every assignment of which in the file is one bare getMap/getArray). A point read links only from writes to its own map and, when both keys are literal, its own key. Entry sites in test files are dropped (each test builds its own Y.Doc). getMap<T>('x') is now an accessor too.\n\nProduction-path test: test_yjs_entry_reads.py::test_the_survey_links_the_creator_to_the_reader (run_behavior_map). Mutation-tested: key matching, the multi-binding guard, generic calls, the test-file filter.\n\nCorpus A/B (seven Yjs repos, every added edge read): six repos 0 changed; AFFiNE +519: 29 entry edges (workspace meta.name/meta.avatar writers -> electron db adapter / IPC handler / profile worker readers; spaces subdoc set/delete -> idb store / id converter), 28 real flows and one logger-label template literal in the same function as a real read; 490 from getMap<T>() becoming an accessor like non-generic getMap().\n\nStill out of scope, as stated: the object -> Y.Doc hop (runtime string). Known limit: a chain split across lines is not seen."  # 14a2
